{"name":"Black Garnet","hex":"#4e4444","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"garnet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard transparent mineral that is often used as gemstones and abrasives.","A dark red color, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garnet"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Genius: Black Garnet","blocks":[{"text":"The Genius: Black Garnet is the third season of The Genius. It debuted on tvN on October 1, 2014."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Genius%3A_Black_Garnet"},{"title":"Garnet","blocks":[{"text":"Garnets are a group of silicate minerals that have been used since the Bronze Age as gemstones and abrasives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Garnet_Andradite20.jpg/330px-Garnet_Andradite20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garnet"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co